    Review: show precise plate-checker scores, cutoff and actual source-frame provenance (#90)
    
    * Bind secondary plate scores to the exact source frame that was checked
    
    * Include exact detector source frame with saved secondary model score
    
    * Include exact detector source frame with saved secondary model score
    
    * Show precise raw checker score and cutoff for actual representative frame, not another sighting
    
    * Style raw verifier scores and distinguish borrowed previews from scored detector frames
    
    * Keep Review representative checker score tied to its own source detection
    
    * Regress exact verifier source-frame provenance in both model modes
    
    * Regress tiny raw-score display and prevent group frame score transplants in Review
    
    * Disclose that Review groups share relative corners instead of optically tracking plate shape
    
    * Keep group disclosure accurate before and after source-frame-safe geometry PR #70
    
    * Explain exact-frame checker scores and raw cutoff in Review docs
    
    * Clarify grouped detections vs optical plate-corner tracking
    
    * Label original detector confidence separately from raw secondary checker score
    
    * Test detector vs checker labels and honest Review track-group wording
    
    * Keep Review grids immediately after category headers to preserve filtering and image preloading
    
    * Make manual plate-tracker instructions truthful about box tracking vs perspective corners
    
    * Keep manual plate tracker instructions distinct from true per-frame corner tracking

